73. (1) Notwithstanding anything contained in the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973, where an order is passed under sub-section (1) of section 72, an appeal shall lie, both on facts and on law from (a) the order made by the District Commission to the State Commission;
(b) the order made by the State Commission to the National Commission; and ( c ) t h e o r d e r m a d e b y t h e N a t i o n a l C o m m i s s i o n t o t h e S u p r e m e C o u r t . 
